  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Uke-Shogi. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Uke-Shogi is a Japanese defensive card game inspired by Shogi (Japanese Chess) concepts. The 'Uke' (受け) refers to defense. Players use standard cards to represent chess-like pieces, focusing on defensive positioning and piece capture mechanics. A niche hybrid of card and board game concepts.",
    objective: 'Be the first player to play all your cards (empty your hand) to win the deal. Players take turns matching the current lead card or passing; the last player to match plays a new card until one player runs out.',
    gameplay: "Cards represent Shogi pieces with specific movement rules. Focus on defensive (Uke) strategy. Captured cards can be redeployed (drop mechanic from Shogi). Promotion possible when reaching opponent's territory.",
